<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="66063" href="schedule/2019/spring/FR/335/66063.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="FR" href="schedule/2019/spring/FR.xml">French</subject><course id="335" href="schedule/2019/spring/FR/335.xml">French Cultural History to 1789</course></parents><sectionNumber>B  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>In this course we study the social and cultural history of France from its beginnings to the end of the eighteenth century in a European and global context. The goal is to provide students with a thorough understanding of major social developments and cultural movements that both characterize pre-revolutionary France and have left their indelible mark on modern French society. Readings and class discussion in French.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G20</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Keller" firstName="M">Keller, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>